 > linebreak nicely. dvi-based methods just crawl away in despair and =
make
 > a long unbroken link. People do claim they could break links at the =
dvi
 > level, but I don't think anyone has actually done it

is that technically very different from providing, say, color support at =
dvi
level? i mean if i say \textcolor{red}{this text is in red} and my text =
gets
broken across the line by TeX all that TeX does is providing some =
\special at
the begin and end of this text (ie they fall onto two different
lines). Nevertheless dvips can color my text red.

so why can't i let TeX split the link and nevertheless communicate via
\specials to, say dvips what the unbroken link would be?

do i miss something?

frank

